  "chapter": 477,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 48 Chapter 477\n \n      MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 6884-B, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the general business law and the vehicle and traf-\n        fic law, in relation  to  requiring  automobile  brokers  to  be\n        licensed\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  Individuals  seeking to purchase a car often retain the services of an\nautomobile broker. Automobile brokers work directly with dealerships  to\nnegotiate  a  sale  for  their clients, and receive a flat fee for their\nservices. This legislation would establish  a  process  for  registering\nautomobile brokers with the New York State Department of Motor Vehicles,\nand  implement  certain  safeguards  to prevent unlawful deceptive prac-\ntices.\n\n  I strongly support the intent of this bill, as it  would  regulate  an\nindustry  that  currently  operates  without  any  specific registration\nrequirements. As originally drafted, however, the bill has certain tech-\nnical and administrative concerns that would make it difficult to imple-\nment effectively. The Executive has secured an agreement with the Legis-\nlature to pass  legislation  in  the  upcoming  legislative  session  to\naddress these concerns, as well as to strengthen the consumer notice and\ndisclosure  requirements included in the original bill. On that basis, I\nam signing this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2017
 },
